\details{
This \code{\link{fe_inventory}} object was derived from a simulated
forest enterprise (pure spruce, 400 stands, 5 ha each). It contains a
10-plot subsample selected for unique within-plot tree IDs. The original
simulation tree IDs are used as \code{lfd_bhd}, making the BaySF tree ID
(\code{paste(lfd_satz, lfd_bhd)}) a permanent identifier that is stable
across inventories. This enables testing of \code{tree_id_style = "generic"}
(ID-based matching) in \code{\link{inv_increment_repsurv_ccirc}}.

Seven of the ten plots have both vanished and ingrown trees; three plots
have all trees surviving between surveys. The dataset represents the
first survey (year 2020). See
\code{\link{data_ex5_sample_fe_inventory}} for the second survey.

Generated by \code{data-raw/simulated_inventory_generic_matching.R}.
